# Architecture

This app is Next.js 16 with `cacheComponents` and `partialPrefetching` already on. Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before adding a framework API. Do not add the Pages Router, `middleware.ts`, or the pre-Cache Components `unstable_cache` model. Request interception belongs in root `proxy.ts`, and only for redirects or headers.

## Shape

- Routes live in `app/`. Marketing pages are Server Components. Client Components are leaves for forms, menus, and other interaction.
- Group URLs without changing them: `app/(marketing)` and `app/(admin)`. Non-routes go in `_components` or `lib/`.
- Public lead capture is a Server Action. Admin mutations are Server Actions. Webhooks from Resend and Twilio are Route Handlers.
- Put reads and writes in a server-only data access layer under `lib/dal`. Pages receive DTOs, not Prisma rows.
- Marketing pages may use `use cache` with an explicit `cacheLife`. Lead, admin, and webhook paths stay dynamic.

## Scale

- One shared header, footer, and lead form. Suburb pages pass city content into that shell.
- Ship the seller site before the blog editor and before any property-listing UI.
- Keep acquired-home inventory off the seller navigation.

```tsx
// app/(marketing)/stop-foreclosure/page.tsx
export default async function Page() {
  "use cache";
  cacheLife("hours");
  return <StopForeclosurePage />;
}
```
